# What a change bulkhead-git-check reports can do, so you can judge it.
# Each line is a shell pattern, then what a match means. The pattern
# matches "KIND:WHAT", e.g., "config:filter.lfs.smudge" or
# "hook:pre-commit"; the first match wins. git prints a key's section
# and name in lower case, so write them that way here. See
# compartments.md, "Git runs commands from local files".
repo:* a repository you hadn't approved: check its settings below, and don't run git in it until you have.
error:* git couldn't read this, so the check can't see what's there; look at it by hand.
git-dir:* where git keeps this repository: a change can mean a planted .git file pointing elsewhere.
push-to:* where a plain git push sends a branch: check you meant to push there.
common-dir:* where git reads this repository's config and hooks: a planted .git/commondir redirects them.
hook:* a hook: git-hook-passthrough runs it only once you approve its hash, but check it anyway.
config:filter.* a filter driver: runs a command when git checks out or adds a file that .gitattributes assigns to it.
config:diff.external runs a command on every git diff.
config:diff.* a diff driver: runs a command when git diffs a file that .gitattributes assigns to it (git diff --no-ext-diff --no-textconv avoids it).
config:merge.* a merge driver: runs a command when git merges a file that .gitattributes assigns to it.
config:url.* rewrites URLs: can send your fetch or push, and its credentials, elsewhere.
config:remote.*.uploadpack runs a command on fetch from a local or ssh remote.
config:remote.*.receivepack runs a command on push to a local or ssh remote.
config:remote.*.vcs runs the remote helper git-remote-VCS.
config:remote.*.mirror makes a push mirror every ref, deleting the remote's other branches.
config:remote.*.push picks what a push sends and where it lands.
config:remote.* a remote's settings: most only affect fetch, but check it in git-config(1).
config:http.* HTTP settings (maybe for one URL): e.g., a proxy, extra headers, or turning off certificate checks.
config:credential.* credential helpers: git gives each one your password, so a planted one can steal it.
config:include.* includes another file's settings: check that file too (its settings are listed here as well).
config:includeif.* includes another file's settings: check that file too (its settings are listed here as well).
config:core.fsmonitor runs a command on most git commands (your login environment pins it, but cron and the like don't get that).
config:core.hookspath picks where hooks come from (your login environment pins it).
config:core.sshcommand runs a command to reach ssh remotes.
config:core.gitproxy runs a command to reach git:// remotes.
config:core.pager runs a command to show git's output.
config:core.editor runs a command when git wants a message from you.
config:core.askpass runs a command to ask for your password.
config:core.worktree makes git work on another directory.
config:core.* a core setting: most are harmless, but check it in git-config(1).
config:sequence.editor runs a command during git rebase -i.
config:pager.* runs a command to show some git command's output.
config:alias.* an alias: one starting with "!" runs a command when you use the alias.
config:gpg.* picks the program git runs to sign or verify.
config:protocol.* allows or refuses ways to reach remotes (ext:: runs a command).
config:submodule.* a submodule's settings: an update starting with "!" runs a command, and a URL picks where it fetches.
config:uploadpack.* settings for serving fetches: packobjectshook runs a command.
config:* not one I know to be risky; check it in git-config(1).
